  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-01-19T09:51:44.675Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I was creating a local third-person camera perspective for an OSC-powered avatar I'm making atm, and I noticed that parts of the avatar that utilized the Roll setting of a LookAt constraint caused the clone in the MirrorReflection layer to fail and ignore the value set by an animation, at least locally. This caused the clone to desync from my actual avatar and show two copies of it in my camera. I didn't test whether it occurs remotely since no-one else had a camera setup to check with. \n\nHowever, the rest of the constraint works as expected, in that it correctly points the local Z axis at the source object. This makes me think that whatever code that controls the clone may simply not be setting it. I'd have to set the roll to a static value and check again to be sure if that's the case, or if animating the value is breaking it elsewhere.\n\nCulling out the MirrorReflection or LocalPlayer layer on my camera is not viable for me either since it breaks certain worlds that utilize either or both layers significantly, such as the Udon Duck Park map.",
